    "prompt_additions": "Ghana Acts use continuous arabic section numbering that does not restart per Part. Complex codifying acts (e.g., Companies Act) may use Chapter > Part > Section with chapters named by ordinal words (CHAPTER ONE). Sections are always cited as 'section N', never 'article N', except in the Constitution where 'Article N' is used."
